review_basis = "The audited source is the supplied base revision; the pre-existing task-status and graph-ignore changes do not alter members. One handwritten Rust test file was read in full. Twenty-eight generated upstream response recordings take the BRIEF generated-data exception, with every envelope/body loaded and per-file provenance and shape notes; no generated data is claimed as clean source."
qualification_boundary = "This is an audit record, not a dependency upgrade or an inventory-target repair. req.22108 ac_1 governs dependency alert disposition and req.22998 ac_1 requires original target evidence for a repair. Record validation does not certify the Rust suite, frozen dependency install, live explorer or all network behavior."
lifecycle_security = "The sixteen consumed rows are read-only HTTP endpoints with no persistent state in this slice. Paths, methods, encodings and shared response models were compared against local routes/controllers/views; findings name disagreements and absent failure coverage. Captures contain no bearer credential or private signing key. Opaque metadata/source/URL response content is not executed. Backend persistence, tenancy and restart are not exercised by replay; shared test-server lifecycle is a separate finding."
retired_references = "No active retired router, daemon or LayerX method reference was found in member source or recording envelopes; Ethereum recordings are compatibility samples rather than deployed Paxeer defaults. Retired architecture, endpoint and settlement references in the package documentation are recorded separately."

